# Scenario: does a colony's whole era survive with the burrow machinery armed?
#
# One line per server console command. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# `@wait <marker>` blocks until that text appears in the server log.
#
# What this actually exercises, and what it cannot:
#   - Colony founding, digging, link recording - and through record(), the
#     reconciler's linkChanged notify. With no player in the burrow no chunk
#     down there is ever loaded, so every notify must be a cheap no-op: this
#     scenario is the NULL-PATH soak for the whole burrow stack. A leak, a
#     growing queue, or a tick-time creep here is a bug in the notify path
#     itself, because nothing below should be doing any work at all.
#   - The fortress mound: the core mound of each colony should carry the
#     FORTRESS state after its first trips.
#   - The giant-mole trip bridge, same null path: trips fire, nobody is below,
#     no traversal must ever spawn.
#   - NOT exercised: burrow chunk reconciliation, decoration, creature spawns,
#     the traversal entity itself. All of those need a player below and belong
#     to the in-game checklist, not to a headless soak.

forceload add -512 -128 -257 127
forceload add -256 -128 -1 127
forceload add 0 -128 255 127
forceload add 256 -128 511 127

say SOAK-CHECK empty-world
moleverse colony list

# Three founding pairs, far enough apart for three colonies.
summon moleverse:mole -350 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole -345 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 0 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 5 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 350 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 355 -2 0

# Two hours of game time. Colonies found, spread, dig their networks, and the
# burrow-side notifies fire thousands of times into the void.
tick sprint 144000
@wait Sprint complete

say SOAK-CHECK after-era
moleverse colony list
moleverse burrow info

# The questions this run answers, read from the log afterwards:
#   - colony count stable at 3 (separation held)?
#   - link counts grown and pruned sanely?
#   - no Exception, no Ticking entity, no growing "queue" figures in the
#     reconciler's dev log lines (devLogging is on in every gradle run)?
#   - tick time at the end comparable to the start?
say SOAK-DONE
